# Backend-to-Frontend Integration Rules

## Frontend Reference
Frontend repository: `/Users/sami/project/vero/Alexandriauiv3`

## Contract Guarantees for UI Consumers
- Keep response shapes predictable and JSON-serializable.
- Keep status code semantics stable (validation, permission, not-found, internal error classes).
- Preserve workspace/tenant scoping behavior expected by frontend request flows.
- For long-running operations, keep explicit async/job-style flow semantics when applicable.

## Change Coordination Rules
- If backend request/response schema changes, update frontend handling and both repos' `.cursor/rules/` in the same branch.
- Do not ship breaking API contract changes without coordinated frontend updates.
- Keep migration notes for transitional compatibility behavior when contract changes are unavoidable.

## Ongoing Rules Maintenance Triggers
Update `.cursor/rules/` here whenever any of the following changes:
- endpoint contracts, status semantics, or error payload shapes
- tenant/workspace handling behavior
- cache key versioning strategy tied to prompts/models/pipelines
- feature module boundaries or core architecture conventions
- test policy changes that affect expected development workflow

## Regular Cleaning Policy
- Weekly quick hygiene pass: remove stale references and dead guidance.
- Monthly deep cleanup: deduplicate, tighten wording, and split oversized rules.
- Quarterly audit: verify guidance matches current backend code and frontend integration behavior.

Definition of clean:
- no duplicate or contradictory guidance
- no stale references to removed routes/modules/env vars
- cross-repo rules remain aligned with frontend expectations
- concise, high-signal instructions for day-to-day coding
